senses.gloss:
--People of an eastern kingdom; a mountain kingdom; defeated by Bharata and purified of sin by the worship of Hari;
1: भा. IX. २०. ३०; II. 4. १८; Br. II. १६. १२ and ५१, ६०. ६८; M. ११४. ५६; १२१. ४९; वा. ४५. ८२; १२०. १३६; ४७-48; ५८. ८३.
vanquished by Kalki;
2: Br. II. १८. ५०; III. ७३. १०९; IV. २९. १३१ and १३५; वा. ९८. १०८.
a hill tribe.
3: Br. II. १६. ६८; III. ४८-49; IV. 7. १९; M. ११४. ११ and ३५.
Defeated by Sagara, took caves and hills as residences;
4: Br. III. ४८. २३-49.
reside on the east of भारतवर्ष;
5: Vi. II. 3. 8.
co-habitation with किरात women by a ब्राह्मण; purification at the end of the twelfth day--rites cited.
6: Br. IV. 8. 9.

(V)--a देवी attending on Soma;
1: Br. III. ६५. २६. वा. ९०. २५.
wife of Jayanta; left him for Soma;
2: M. २३. २५.
in the गेयचक्र of ललिता Devi1.
3: Br. IV. १९. ७१.
